    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8866": {
      "title": "Admissions Representative - Undergraduate Admissions",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Admissions Representative - Undergraduate Admissions Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Admissions Representative - Undergraduate Admissions Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Admissions Representative - Undergraduate Admissions Job Description The Admissions Representative – Undergraduate Admissions position assists prospective students and their parents interested in Ashland University through the enrollment process, and to coordinate all college fairs and travel for Undergraduate Admissions, and create communication for those who influence first-year students. Serves as the primary contact for prospective traditional first-year students and their influencers within specific geographic recruitment area. Travels to visit high schools in assigned recruitment area. Travels to attend college day/night programs within assigned recruitment area. Hosts virtual college information programs in targeted recruitment areas. Assists with campus visit programs throughout the year. Serves as a liaison to the Ashbrook and Honors programs. Serves as a liaison to the Office of Student Success. Serves as a liaison to the College of Arts & Sciences and other campus offices for new student recruitment purposes. Serves as a member of the Office of Admissions Leadership Team. Conducts on-campus personal visits and group visit presentations for prospective students and their guests. Assists Director of Admissions with data analysis through utilization of Othot & Slate, including weekly enrollment reporting. Responsible for knowledge of the Slate CRM for communication with prospective students. Effective interpersonal and public speaking communication skills. Willingness to work evenings, weekends or as needed. Ability to work unsupervised. Ability to understand and utilize various technology tools for student recruitment and data analytics. Commitment to diversity and inclusion. Evidence of collaboration within a campus community. Able to communicate with a wide variety of individuals both on and off campus. Willingness to travel extensively during the fall and spring months. Responsible for knowledge of the Slate CRM for communication with prospective students. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from a regionally accredited university. Must have a valid driver’s license. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Some lifting. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 10/05/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1133P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 10/05/2026 Job Open Date 08/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8751 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
