    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8826": {
      "title": "Part-Time Administrative Assistant - Ashbrook Center",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Part-Time Administrative Assistant - Ashbrook Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Part-Time Administrative Assistant - Ashbrook Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Part-Time Administrative Assistant - Ashbrook Center Job Description We are seeking a dependable, organized, and proactive Part-Time Administrative Assistant to support the day-to-day operations of the Ashbrook Center. The ideal candidate is a self-starter who can work independently, prioritize responsibilities, and provide professional and welcoming support to staff, interns, and visitors. Duties include, but are not limited to: Answer the main phone line, take messages, and disseminate information to appropriate staff. Order office and kitchen supplies and monitor inventory levels to ensure needed items are available. Monitor interns and assist with assigning and coordinating their workload. Welcome and assist visitors by providing directions, answering questions, and connecting them with appropriate personnel. Manage incoming and outgoing USPS mail and UPS packages. Work with related departments to execute tasks and provide administrative support as needed. Ensure the smooth and efficient operation of the Ashbrook workroom and intern suite. Perform other administrative duties and special projects as assigned. Required Qualifications Two plus (2+) years professional office experience required. Detail oriented, self-motivated and able to take initiative with minimal supervision. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Professional, friendly, and dependable demeanor. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks and work effectively in an active office environment. Comfortable working with staff, interns, visitors, and colleagues across departments. Knowledge of general office software and equipment usage. Experience in non-profit fundraising or marketing experience a plus, but no prior experience in these fields is required. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 10/01/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 25 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1142P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Job Open Date 09/02/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8825 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
