    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8859": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar - Registrar&#39;s Office",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Associate Registrar - Registrar&#39;s Office Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Associate Registrar - Registrar's Office Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Associate Registrar - Registrar's Office Job Description Ashland University invites applications for the Associate Registrar position. The Associate Registrar is a full time, year-round position. The successful candidate will demonstrate the ways in which they bring value to and will work towards supporting a broadly diverse community. The Associate Registrar oversees daily operations within the Office of the Registrar, leading the office in continuous process and procedure improvements, and implementing best practices. In addition, the Associate Registrar provides leadership, direction, and guidance to office staff; changes in technology, and efforts to provide seamless service and support to our diverse University constituents. The Associate Registrar oversees the publication of the University Course Catalog, coordinating with departments across campus to ensure policies, requirements, and information is up-to-date and accurate. Provides analysis and support for educational policy decisions. Cross-trains with co-workers to provide back-up as needed. This position has direct supervision of the Assistant Registrar. University Records Interprets and clarifies University policies regarding graduation requirements in concert with the Registrar. Serves as Overseer of: verification of degree requirements; production of diplomas and related commencement programs needs Serves as an additional FERPA expert Produces and interprets reports in Informer 5 for Registrar’s office and other stakeholders in tandem with the Assistant Registrar. Staff Leadership Develops and trains staff ensuring consistent communication on academic policy and procedures Contributes to the support, development, and mentorship of staff Assist in the management of the course evaluation policies and procedures of transfer credit for the University. Assist in working with academic departments, admissions, and academic deans to determine AU equivalencies for coursework taken at other institutions Cross-trains and provide back-up support to office colleagues, perform general office duties such as answering the phone, assisting students, faculty and staff, and other duties as assigned. Supervise the day-to-day duties for the Assistant Registrar and other staff. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Five or more years of related registrar office experience. Demonstrated project management skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, and experience using Google Suite. Demonstrated experience learning and utilizing new software programs. Excellent attention to detail, time management, and analytical skills. Strong technical skills with regards to the SIS . Strong written and verbal communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills. Experience engaging and supporting a diverse learning community. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. Experience with Colleague, Coursedog, Softdocs (Etrieve). Physical Demands Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 10/12/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1148P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 10/12/2026 Job Open Date 09/17/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8858 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
