    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8949": {
      "title": "Recruitment Specialist, Master of Arts in American History and Government - Ashbrook Center",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Recruitment Specialist, Master of Arts in American History and Government - Ashbrook Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Recruitment Specialist, Master of Arts in American History and Government - Ashbrook Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Recruitment Specialist, Master of Arts in American History and Government - Ashbrook Center Job Description The Ashbrook Center, an independent center at Ashland University, seeks a Recruitment Specialist for the Master of Arts in American History and Government. Reporting to the Marketing Manager for Ashbrook’s Teacher Programs, this position will promote the recruitment of new students by identifying and executing in-person recruitment opportunities across the country. Marketing and Relationship Management with Local Educational Agencies (25%) Develops and maintains relationships with school districts, regional educational service agencies, charter school networks, and other organizations to promote the program and demonstrate the ways in which it can promote the goals of those organizations. Collaborates with such agencies to market the program and courses to their teachers. Negotiates agreements and bulk enrollment pathways. Provides ongoing stewardship to LEA partners. Marketing and Relationship Management with Individual Prospective Students (75%) Serves as primary in-person recruiter for graduate students, coordinating closely with the Marketing Manager for Ashbrook’s Teacher Programs as well as the Director of the MAHG Program to advance prospective students from the prospect stage through the inquiry and application stages. Attends and assists in the operation of MAHG’s summer residential program in order to engage with current students and gain insights into the character of the program and those it serves. Seeks out and markets to individual students at in-person events, including Teaching American History One Day and Weekend Seminars as well as teacher seminars hosted by university civics centers and other organizations throughout the year and across the country. Identifies opportunities for on-the-ground marketing, seeking conferences and meetings at which large numbers of social studies teachers and K-12 curriculum officers will be present. Attends such gatherings to actively prospect for applicants. Collaborates with Ashbrook’s Teacher Programs team and outside consultants to coordinate marketing strategies. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Experience with marketing and sales OR in higher education marketing and recruitment. Willingness and ability to travel frequently to seminars, conferences and education events around the country. Ability to work on-location in Ashland, OH for a 4-week period each summer. Self-proficiency utilizing a variety of apps and technology, including CRM platforms, digital communications, social media, word processing, marketing design, and presentations. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Able to work independently and to meet performance goals with minimal supervision. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. Five (5) or more years experience as a secondary school social studies teacher, district or regional curriculum coordinator, or related experience in K-12 education. Experience recruiting for a graduate-level program for an adult professional audience. Familiarity with Slate, HubSpot, Canva, and Google Apps. Physical Demands Travel required – four (4) weeks in Ashland, Ohio during June and July. Biweekly travel to conference sites, prospecting, and stewardship with LEA partners. Some lifting required of marketing materials and trade show displays. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 12/15/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1159P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 12/16/2026 Job Open Date 10/19/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8946 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8320": {
      "title": "Casual Bartender - Catering &amp; Conferences",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Casual Bartender - Catering &amp; Conferences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Casual Bartender - Catering & Conferences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Rate of pay for this position is $15.00/hr. Position Details Position Information Position Title Casual Bartender - Catering & Conferences Job Description Bartender for catered events such as wedding receptions, corporate holiday parties, and University functions. Bartenders set up and pull their own bars for each event. All bars are mobile, requiring the pulling and restocking of all alcohol, mixers, and garnishes before and after each event. Bartenders serve cocktails, beer, and wine. Required Qualifications Must be 21 years or older. Qualified candidates must possess natural ability to serve guests in an upscale dining environment. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Bartending experience preferred but not required. Experience handling cash and credit cards preferred but not required. Physical Demands Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 05/18/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 10 Shift Required? Varied Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S095P Number of Vacancies 10 Desired Start Date 05/18/2026 Job Open Date 08/02/2024 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Rate of pay for this position is $15.00/hr. Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/827 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.8