    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8710": {
      "title": "Casual Talon Transport Drivers - Student Affairs",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Casual Talon Transport Drivers - Student Affairs Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Casual Talon Transport Drivers - Student Affairs Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Rate of pay for this position is $14.00 per hour. Position Details Position Information Position Title Casual Talon Transport Drivers - Student Affairs Job Description Ashland University is seeking dependable, friendly drivers to join our Talon Transport team. Drivers provide transportation for students, faculty, and staff to destinations throughout Ohio, including airports, medical appointments, internships, government offices, and more. If you enjoy driving and making a difference in the student experience, we’d love to hear from you! Position Details: Flexible, ride-based schedule—claim trips that fit your availability. Minimum commitment of 2 rides per month. Drive a university-owned SUV covered by AU insurance. Required Qualifications Minimum five (5) years of driving experience. Valid driver’s license. Clean driving record. Responsible, patient, and dependable. Comfortable interacting with students from diverse backgrounds. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Ability to sit for two (2) or more hours at a time. Able to open and close car doors. Able to access and respond to electronic notifications. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 08/31/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 1-5 Shift Required? Varied Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1116P Number of Vacancies 10 Desired Start Date 08/31/2026 Job Open Date 07/14/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Rate of pay for this position is $14.00 per hour. Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8617 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8881": {
      "title": "Director of Student Activities - Office of Student &amp; Residence Life",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Director of Student Activities - Office of Student &amp; Residence Life Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Director of Student Activities - Office of Student & Residence Life Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Director of Student Activities - Office of Student & Residence Life Job Description As a key member of Student Life and Success at Ashland University, the Director of Student Activities is responsible for creating significant opportunities for student engagement that foster a sense of belonging, learning and personal/professional growth, while also aiding in student retention. Coordinate/plan, implement and evaluate traditional campus-wide events including the Involvement Fair, Welcome Tent, Week of Welcome, Homecoming, and Springfest, among others. Advise the Campus Activities Board, the primary student programming organization. Primary responsibilities include supervision, selection, contract negotiation, program implementation and evaluation. In addition, the advisor assists in recruitment, selection, training, and holistic development of CAB members and attends campus events. Advise the Technical Productions Crew, the student led organization whose main function is to provide sound, stage and lighting for campus programs. Advise the Activities, Budgeting, and Chartering Committee ( ABCC ) of Student Senate on matters of chartering and funding. Serve as historian and non-voting member. Provide budget oversight for all student organization funding. Serve as the staff liaison for 100+ student organizations. Implement annual processes including roster updates to Engage, provisional and full charter applications, and funding requests, etc. Maintain Student Organization Manual. Create, implement, and assess training for student organizations to include student organization policies, procedures, and utilization of Engage Ashland software. Manage Engage Ashland software, Engage Ashland Instagram account and create publicity materials to increase use of these platforms. Approve events and forms submitted through Engage. Manage Student Organization Resource Room and all event supplies. Host Programming Team meetings and maintain programming calendar. Assist with Orientation programs and serve as support during the implementation of orientation initiatives, including June/July Summer Orientation Days and Orientation Weekend. Co-facilitate annual Hazing Prevention training session during Orientation Weekend. Plan and facilitate annual Leadership & Service awards program. Attend annual NACA conference with a student delegation. Supervise undergraduate intern. Serve on Strategic Planning Team, Theme 3B: Modernize and reimagine residential living and programming to enhance recruitment, retention, and student satisfaction. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required plus a minimum of two (2) years full-time, professional experience in a college setting. Effective use of organizational and planning skills with attention to detail and follow through. Ability to build positive and meaningful rapport with students. Maintain confidentiality of work-related information and materials. Ability to work as an individual and as a member of a team. Mandatory Title IX reporter. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Prior professional experience in college student programming and advising student organizations, contract negotiation, and budget management. Candidate should consider living near Ashland, Ohio as this position does require frequent evening and weekend hours. Physical Demands Evening and weekend hours. Heavy lifting, use of ladders, unloading/loading event trucks. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 10/05/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1128P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 10/05/2026 Job Open Date 08/17/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8713 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8766": {
      "title": "Principal Faculty for the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies- Part Time - Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Principal Faculty for the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies- Part Time - Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Principal Faculty for the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies- Part Time - Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Principal Faculty for the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies- Part Time - Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences Division College of Nursing (CON) Department Medical Sciences Job Description The Part-Time Principal Faculty member for the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies Program will work closely with the Program Director and Principal Faculty members to implement and maintain the curriculum in accordance with ARC -PA Standards as a course director on a twelve (12) month, part-time basis. As a Course Director the individual is responsible for development, implementation, delivery, and evaluation of assigned courses. The Principal Faculty works collaboratively with faculty within the Dwight Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences and Ashland University. The Part-Time Principal Faculty member is responsible for course development and implementation to ensure the PA students readiness to practice upon graduation. Principal Faculty member responsibilities include: Support the mission of Ashland University and Dwight Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences. Support Ashland University’s philosophy of Accent on the Individual. Development and review of the mission statement of the PA Program. Provide academic instruction. Participates in review and revision of the program competencies. Develops, implements, evaluates and ensures course syllabi maintain compliance with ARC -PA Standards of assigned courses. Review and revision, as necessary, of the program goals and competencies. Participates in developing, reviewing, and revising as necessary the mission statement for the program. Participates in evaluating student performances. Participate in the program’s ongoing self-assessment, analysis, and accreditation processes with primary responsibility for didactic education components. Is familiar with ARC -PA accreditation standards and assists in providing documented compliance. Participate in the development and maintenance of the didactic year sections of the student handbook. Participate in the design and implementation of summative examinations. Serve as an academic advisor to students. Provide remedial instruction of didactic year students. Participate in the admissions process including student recruitment and selection. Participate as a member of PA program committees as assigned by the PA Program Director. Participate in state and national PA organizations as necessary to promote the program and the profession. Participates in professional development activities outside of Ashland University’s PA program in areas of clinical practice, scholarly activities or advancement of educational degree as agreed upon by the Program Director. Agrees to not participate as a health care provider for students in the program, except in an emergency situation. Perform other duties as determined by negotiation at the annual performance review by the Program Director. Required Qualifications Master’s degree or higher is required. Certification and Licensure requirements specific to discipline. Minimum of three (3) years of clinical experience consistent with academic preparation. Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching and/or administrative experience in PA education or healthcare-related field. Demonstrated organizational and leadership skills. Ability to build collegial relationships. Active service or leadership at the local, regional, or national level. Active engagement in scholarly work consistent with academic preparation and clinical expertise. Physical Demands The Principal Faculty member should be available to participate in events important to the ongoing success of the University and College. Requires the ability to work indoors in a moderately stressful environment and the ability to adapt to changes in workload. Physical requirements may include frequent sitting, walking, lifting, reaching, pushing/pulling, and twisting. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 09/01/2026 Proposed Rank Clinical Assistant Tenure-Track No Service Basis 12 month, Part Time Fixed Term Yes Term Start Date 09/01/2026 Term End Date 05/31/2027 Benefits No Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number F129P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Job Open Date 08/24/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8765 Reference Collection References Minimum Requests Maximum Requests Recommendation Deadline Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
