    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8848": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant - Professional Learning Services, Columbus OH Center",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Administrative Assistant - Professional Learning Services, Columbus OH Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Administrative Assistant - Professional Learning Services, Columbus OH Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Administrative Assistant - Professional Learning Services, Columbus OH Center Job Description This full-time position is under the supervision of and reports to the Director of Professional Learning Services ( PLS ) at Ashland University’s Columbus, OH Center. The Administrative Assistant provides support services to PLS . Completes administrative office and clerical work including serving as a resource person to inform interested individuals about PLS . Assigns and maintains class numbering system and database. Prepares and forwards agreement forms to school districts and vendors. Enters registrations into computer system. Processes credit/debit card and check payments. Balances payment records and forwards to business office. Maintains files on grade sheets, syllabi, and contracts. Creates and updates the class schedule on the web page. Updates and maintains the web page information. Responds daily to email communications. Prepares reports under the direction of the Director. Demonstrates necessary human relations skills in order to maintain a friendly, helpful atmosphere working with instructors, students, and school district personnel. Maintains current and accurate records on the computer. Maintains sufficient office supplies/forms for PLS . Prepares regular mailings to superintendents, curriculum directors, adjuncts, and others for PLS via US Mail and email. Processes check requests and supplement contracts for PLS . Performs other duties requested by the Director. Required Qualifications Minimum of a high school diploma. Experience as an administrative assistant in a university or school setting desired. Ability to work at both the Ashland University Main Campus and Columbus OH Center . Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Associates or Bachelor’s Degree in an associated field of education. Physical Demands An eight (8) hour workday with some flexible scheduling. Subject to frequent interruptions. Extensive use of computer and keyboard. The physical conditioning necessary for sitting for prolonged periods of time. Visual acuity to review written documents. Ability to hear and understand speech in face-to-face contact and on the phone. Manual dexterity to operate telephone and keyboard. Occasionally assist with classroom set-up (rearranging tables and chairs, technology, etc.) Ability to lift file storage boxes. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 09/28/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1147P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 09/28/2026 Job Open Date 09/14/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8846 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
