    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/9001": {
      "title": "Payroll Clerk",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Payroll Clerk Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Payroll Clerk Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Payroll Clerk Job Description Ashland University’s Business Office seeks to fill a full-time Payroll Clerk position. Under the supervision of the Payroll Manager, this position performs the day to day operations of the Payroll department including timely processing and payment of personnel salaries and wages, maintaining effective internal controls accordance with Ashland University policies as well as compliance with applicable laws and regulations. This position must also to place accent on the individual with its communication to employees to help resolve requests and discrepancies inquired of. Essential Position Duties and Responsibilities: Processes and verifies the accuracy of data for the semi-monthly salaried, bi-weekly hourly, supplemental and student payrolls. Ensures approved hours are properly imported and calculated in regards to bi-weekly and student payrolls from multiple sources. Verifies state and local taxes are calculated based on the appropriate location worked. Processes and maintains garnishment and child support orders. Inputs and reconciles various voluntary benefit deductions. Maintains employee tax and direct deposit information for new and existing employees. Assists employees regarding payroll questions both verbally and written communication. Monitors contracts submitted to the payroll office through Sharepoint and other means. Works closely with Payroll Manager, Human Resources staff and Controller to coordinate the function of the Business and Human Resources Departments. Maintains employee confidence and protects payroll operations by keeping information confidential. Contributes to team effort by accomplishing related results as needed. Required Qualifications Associate’s Degree or Bachelor of Science or Arts in Business or its related fields from an accredited College or University. Knowledge of rules and regulations impacting federal, state and local levels. Multi-state payroll experience is a plus. Proficient with Microsoft Office Suite software. Ability to manage multiple assignments, projects; meet deadlines, uses sound judgement, and interprets laws and regulations. High attention to detail, effective organization and planning. Excellent oral and written communication, analytical, problem-solving, critical thinking and interpersonal skills. Ability to work after hours and weekends as needed. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications One (1) to three (3) years experience of payroll processing is preferred. Experience in higher education industry is preferred. Knowledge of Ellucian Colleague system and Kronos is preferred. Physical Demands Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 11/09/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1156P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 11/09/2026 Job Open Date Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8913 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/9003": {
      "title": "Director, MFA in Creative Writing/Assistant Professor of English, Non-Tenure Track - College of Arts and Sciences",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Director, MFA in Creative Writing/Assistant Professor of English, Non-Tenure Track - College of Arts and Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Director, MFA in Creative Writing/Assistant Professor of English, Non-Tenure Track - College of Arts and Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Director, MFA in Creative Writing/Assistant Professor of English, Non-Tenure Track - College of Arts and Sciences Division College of Arts & Sciences (CAS) Department English Job Description The Department of English and Foreign Languages at Ashland University ( www.ashland.edu ) invites applications for Director of the Master of Fine Arts ( MFA ) in Creative Writing and Assistant or Associate Professor of English, Non-Tenure Track. Directing the Ashland Poetry Press is included as part of this assignment. Housed within the College of Arts & Sciences, this position reports to both the Department Chair and the College Dean. This position is on a 9-month contract with a stipend to direct the summer residency for MFA . The successful candidate will have an emphasis in creative writing, demonstrate excellence in teaching, have a strong commitment to undergraduate and graduate education, and possess leadership and administrative skills. Furthermore, the candidate will have significant publications and an active agenda of creative projects. The candidate is expected to contribute to the life of Ashland University through active engagement and service. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in creative writing, and graduate courses or other courses in the department as needed. The full- time, in-person faculty position includes 9 credit hours per year of teaching and 15 credits of course release for directing the MFA program and the Ashland Poetry Press. The MFA includes year-round planning and recruiting for a 10-day summer residency on campus; supervision of a part-time assistant; coordination with admissions, marketing, and advising; as well as budgeting and enrollment management for the program. The position could start as early as May 2027. Required Qualifications MFA or Ph.D. in English (or related field) required. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D or MFA with an emphasis in Creative Writing, particularly poetry. Ability to teach courses in American Literature would be an added benefit. Physical Demands Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 08/23/2027 Proposed Rank Assistant Tenure-Track No Service Basis 9 month, Other(please specify) - Summer stipend paid seperately Fixed Term Term Start Date 08/23/2027 Term End Date 05/12/2028 Benefits Yes Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number F135P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/23/2027 Job Open Date 10/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8970 Reference Collection References Minimum Requests Maximum Requests Recommendation Deadline Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Letters Of Recommendation Optional Documents 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
