    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8991": {
      "title": "Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Director of Admissions Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Director of Admissions Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Director of Admissions Job Description The Director of Admissions leads the strategy and day-to-day execution of Ashland University’s traditional undergraduate, international, online and graduate admissions programs. The Director translates university enrollment priorities into a clear annual recruitment plan, builds a reliable prospective-student pipeline, develops the admissions team, and uses timely evidence to adjust work throughout the cycle. The role is accountable for recruitment performance and prospective student experience, while partnering with Enrollment Management leadership and campus colleagues on enrollment, net tuition revenue, affordability, and student-fit goals. Reporting to the Vice President of Enrollment Management, the Director serves on the Enrollment Management Leadership Team and leads professional admissions staff, student tour guides, and admissions ambassadors. The Director combines strategic planning with visible, hands-on leadership in territory recruitment, campus visits, and signature events. Key Responsibilities Set strategy and turn it into action Develop an annual recruitment strategy aligned with enrollment, net tuition revenue, academic, geographic, and student-success priorities. Translate strategy into actionable territory plans, audience segments, outreach channels, event calendars, staff assignments, and funnel goals. Use funnel history and market intelligence to identify opportunities and risks, adjust recruitment efforts during the cycle, and apply lessons to future plans. Lead the admissions team and student recruitment experience Supervise, coach, and develop admissions staff; set clear expectations and strengthen their recruitment, communication, CRM , and data skills. Assign territories and responsibilities based on institutional priorities, market opportunity, and team capacity. Lead a welcoming, coordinated prospective student experience across visits, events, outreach, and partnerships with families, counselors, academic units, and campus offices. Manage performance, forecasting, and continuous improvement Maintain a stage-by-stage enrollment forecast; explain gaps from plan and recommend specific actions to address them. Use CRM , student information, event, and reporting systems to support accurate data, timely outreach, and useful analysis. Evaluate recruitment results, costs, student feedback, and revenue implications; share concise updates and recommend improvements to Enrollment Management leadership. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Experience using data to set priorities, monitor performance, communicate findings, and improve recruitment or service outcomes. Experience leading projects, coordinating complex events, or supervising and coaching employees or student staff. Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, presentation, and relationship-building skills; ability to communicate effectively with students, families, school counselors, colleagues, and community partners. Ability to organize multiple priorities, exercise sound judgment, work independently, and collaborate across a campus community. Valid driver’s license and ability to travel during peak recruitment periods. Availability for occasional evening and weekend work, especially during recruitment events and peak-cycle needs. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications At least five years of full-time experience in undergraduate, international, online or graduate admissions, college access, enrollment management, or a closely related field; progressively responsible experience is preferred. Master’s degree in higher education, student affairs, business, or a related field. Other fields will be considered upon the candidate’s ability to demonstrate relevance to the role. Experience supervising professional admissions staff and student employees. Experience with Slate or a comparable CRM , funnel reporting, recruitment territory design, and enrollment forecasting. Experience managing recruitment budgets and evaluating the return and student impact of recruitment activities. Knowledge of current recruitment practices, financial aid concepts, and the needs of diverse student populations. Physical Demands This is a full-time, exempt administrative position. Work is performed in an office and campus setting with regular interaction across the university and in external recruitment markets. The role requires regional travel, periodic evening and weekend work, and some lifting in support of visits and events. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals to perform the essential functions of the position. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 11/16/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? First Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1160P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 11/16/2026 Job Open Date 10/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8975 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents References Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/9000": {
      "title": "Full-Time Catering Event Supervisor 2 - Catering and Conferences",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Full-Time Catering Event Supervisor 2 - Catering and Conferences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Full-Time Catering Event Supervisor 2 - Catering and Conferences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Full-Time Catering Event Supervisor 2 - Catering and Conferences Job Description Ashland University Catering and Conferences seeks to fill a full-time Catering Event Supervisor position. AU Catering serves a large variety of events from ten (10) guest lunch meetings to three hundred (300) guest off-premise weddings and everything in between. Prepare for events in accordance to the Banquet Event Order ( BEO ). Leads wait staff and bartenders during the event, including assigning set up tasks, sections, and clean up tasks and ensures that all details of the BEO are met. Responsible for overseeing food safety and food quality. Manage bars and bartenders. Schedule varies week to week depending on events, most shifts are nights and weekends. Required Qualifications Hospitality experience. Knowledge of food safety. Customer service experience. Must be twenty-one (21) years of age or older to oversee bars and bartenders. Applicant must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Ashland University will not sponsor or take over sponsorship for an employment visa. Preferred Qualifications Catering experience. Special event experience. Leadership experience. Bartending experience. Physical Demands Some heavy lifting. Standing for long periods of time. Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 11/09/2026 Anticipated Number of Hours Working per Week 40 Shift Required? Varied Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1164P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 11/09/2026 Job Open Date 10/22/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8998 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
