    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/9002": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting, Tenure Track; or Lecturer of Accounting, Non-Tenure Track (Promotable) - Dauch College of Business and Economics",
      "description": "Ashland University Portal | Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting, Tenure Track; or Lecturer of Accounting, Non-Tenure Track (Promotable) - Dauch College of Business and Economics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Ashland University Home Human Resources Home Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting, Tenure Track; or Lecturer of Accounting, Non-Tenure Track (Promotable) - Dauch College of Business and Economics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting, Tenure Track; or Lecturer of Accounting, Non-Tenure Track (Promotable) - Dauch College of Business and Economics Division College of Business & Economics (COBE) Department Accounting Job Description The Dauch College of Business and Economics, Department of Accounting and Management Information Systems, is seeking an Assistant/Associate Professor of Accounting, a tenure-track position, or a Lecturer of Accounting, non-tenure-track position, beginning Fall 2027. Teaching of undergraduate and graduate level courses in accounting include tax, auditing, accounting information systems, and financial accounting. Excellence in teaching is required, as is participation in service activities to the university, community and profession. Assistant/Associate Professor candidates are also expected to conduct scholarly activities in their area of concentration to maintain AACSB Scholarly Academic status. Required Qualifications Candidates for Assistant/Associate Professor would ideally hold an earned doctorate from an AACSB accredited institution in an appropriate field and an active CPA license. Candidates for Lecturer must have a graduate degree in business and an active CPA license. Previous teaching experience, including demonstrated ability to teach effectively in a technology-facilitated environment, as well as in a traditional classroom setting, is a requirement. Preferred Qualifications Strong candidates will have compelling evidence of teaching effectiveness, an active professional or scholarly agenda, and relevant professional work experience. Physical Demands Anticipated Start Date of New Hire 08/23/2027 Proposed Rank Assistant Tenure-Track Yes Service Basis 9 month Fixed Term Yes Term Start Date 08/23/2027 Term End Date 05/12/2028 Benefits Yes Job Duties Posting Detail Information Posting Number F130P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/23/2027 Job Open Date 09/24/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8889 Reference Collection References Minimum Requests Maximum Requests Recommendation Deadline Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Letters Of Recommendation 401 College Avenue Ashland, OH 44805 419.289.4142, 800.882.1548 Athletics Employment Commencement News Center Accessibility Back to top Wellness Consumer Information Student Complaints Campus Store To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
